<title>FINLAND: Merita up as U.S. road show sparks demand.</title>
<headline>Merita up as U.S. road show sparks demand.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish banking group Merita Oy rose sharply on Friday on demand partly sparked by a road show for investors in the U.S. this week, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1220/0920 GMT Merita A stood at 11.20 markka, up 0.50 markka or 4.67 percent in extremely lively trade. Volume was 34.4 million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;Evidently (Merita CEO) Vesa Vainio has been saying good things in America,&quot; one broker said, referring to a newspaper report on the road show.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
